IMPORT prelude

-- State Courts Act 1970 (Singapore) -- which civil claims the District and Magistrates' Courts can hear (ss 19, 52), giving
-- up the excess to stay in the cheaper court (s 22), extending jurisdiction by agreement (s 23), no splitting claims (s 35),
-- and the costs penalty for suing in the High Court when a State Court would have done (s 39).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SCA1970.txt.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 23 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository (s 4 by 9, s 9 by 5). SCOPED to civil
-- jurisdiction and its costs consequences. Not encoded: constitution and officers, bailiffs, criminal jurisdiction beyond
-- its territorial reach, transfers between courts, appeals (see the supreme-court-of-judicature-act-1969 row), and
-- administration.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `State Courts Act 1970 -- civil jurisdiction`

§§ `2, 19, 52 -- the limits`

-- s 2: "District Court limit" means $250,000; "Magistrate's Court limit" means $60,000 (each variable by order).
-- s 19(4): a District Court cannot try an action where the amount claimed, or the value of the subject matter, exceeds its
-- limit. (3): nor exercise supervisory or judicial review jurisdiction, exclusive jurisdiction of another court, or "(ca) any
-- jurisdiction to hear and try an action in PASSING OFF".
-- s 52(1A): a Magistrate's Court cannot try an action "(a) where there is NO CLAIM FOR ANY SUM OF MONEY; (aa) ... in passing
-- off; (b) [over its limit]".
--
-- Passing off is excluded from both State Courts whatever its value. And a Magistrate's Court cannot hear a claim seeking
-- only an injunction or a declaration, however small: it needs a money claim.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the District Court limit` MEANS 250000

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Magistrate's Court limit` MEANS 60000

DECLARE Action HAS
    `amount claimed` IS A NUMBER
    `claims a sum of money` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is passing off` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is judicial review or supervisory` IS A BOOLEAN
    `parties signed a memorandum agreeing to District Court jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `claimant abandons the excess` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the action` IS AN Action
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a District Court can hear the action` IF
        NOT `the action`'s `is passing off`
    AND NOT `the action`'s `is judicial review or supervisory`
    AND (    `the action`'s `amount claimed` AT MOST `the District Court limit`
         OR  `the action`'s `parties signed a memorandum agreeing to District Court jurisdiction`
         OR  `the action`'s `claimant abandons the excess`)

GIVEN `the action` IS AN Action
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Magistrate's Court can hear the action` IF
        `the action`'s `claims a sum of money`
    AND NOT `the action`'s `is passing off`
    AND NOT `the action`'s `is judicial review or supervisory`
    AND `the action`'s `amount claimed` AT MOST `the Magistrate's Court limit`

§§ `22, 23 -- abandoning the excess, or agreeing`

-- s 22(1): a claimant may abandon the excess over the District Court limit, and the District Court then has jurisdiction, but
-- cannot recover more than the limit; (2) "the judgment ... is a FULL DISCHARGE of all demands in respect of the cause of
-- action" -- the abandoned excess is gone for good.
-- s 23: by "a memorandum signed by them or their respective solicitors", the parties may give the District Court jurisdiction
-- with NO upper limit.
GIVEN `the action` IS AN Action
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the claimant can recover in the District Court` MEANS
    IF `the action`'s `parties signed a memorandum agreeing to District Court jurisdiction`
    THEN `the action`'s `amount claimed`
    ELSE IF `the action`'s `amount claimed` GREATER THAN `the District Court limit`
         THEN `the District Court limit`
         ELSE `the action`'s `amount claimed`

GIVEN `abandoned the excess` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the excess can be sued for later` IF
    NOT `abandoned the excess`

§§ `35 -- no splitting`

-- s 35: "A cause of action must not be divided for the purpose of bringing 2 or more actions." A $300,000 claim cannot be
-- split into two $150,000 District Court actions.
GIVEN `actions brought on one cause of action` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim has been impermissibly split` IF
    `actions brought on one cause of action` GREATER THAN 1

§§ `39 -- suing in the High Court when a State Court would do`

-- s 39(1): where an action that "could have been commenced in a State Court" is brought in the High Court, a claimant who
-- recovers no more than the District Court limit gets only District Court costs; no more than the Magistrate's Court limit,
-- only Magistrate's Court costs. (2): the recovery is measured "without regard to any deduction made in respect of
-- CONTRIBUTORY NEGLIGENCE".
--
-- A claimant who proves $300,000 of loss but recovers $200,000 after a one-third contributory-negligence deduction is treated
-- as recovering $300,000 -- and keeps High Court costs.
GIVEN `gross amount before contributory negligence` IS A NUMBER, `could have been brought in a State Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
`the costs scale` MEANS
    IF NOT `could have been brought in a State Court`
    THEN "High Court"
    ELSE IF `gross amount before contributory negligence` AT MOST `the Magistrate's Court limit`
         THEN "Magistrate's Court"
         ELSE IF `gross amount before contributory negligence` AT MOST `the District Court limit`
              THEN "District Court"
              ELSE "High Court"

§§ `50, 51 -- where State Courts' criminal jurisdiction reaches`

-- s 50(2), 51(2): an offence committed (a) within Singapore; (b) on a Singapore-registered ship or aircraft; (c) by a
-- Singapore CITIZEN on the high seas or on any aircraft; or (d) anywhere a written law makes triable in Singapore.
DECLARE Place IS ONE OF
    `in Singapore`
    `on a Singapore ship`
    `by a citizen on the high seas`
    `by a non-citizen on the high seas, foreign ship`
    `abroad, made triable by a written law`
    `abroad, with no such law`

GIVEN `the place` IS A Place
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a State Court has criminal jurisdiction` IF
    CONSIDER `the place`
    WHEN `by a non-citizen on the high seas, foreign ship` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `abroad, with no such law` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
